From fd8b41591d710aec9330f59ebfccbd6c4a9b7228 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 14:41:36 -0700
Subject: test: expect miner-fund, RTT and staking-reward policy parks again

v2/034 rewrote these tests to say "MinerFundPolicy/RTTPolicy parking is
decoupled, PoW chain selection is authoritative". No such decoupling
exists: V2 registers MinerFundPolicy, RTTPolicy and StakingRewardsPolicy
(v2/042 restores soft block parking). The tests had observed the
automatic-unparking bug fixed in the previous eCash commit, which undid
each park immediately.

Restore the upstream park/vote/invalidate expectations, keeping V2's 120s
timing and the 25% staking ratio. abc_feature_minerfund and
abc_p2p_avalanche_policy_minerfund are back to the eCash-tier files.
abc_p2p_avalanche_policy_rtt, abc_p2p_avalanche_policy_stakingrewards and
abc_feature_minerfund pass. abc_mining_rtt now passes the park check and
then stops at the legacy-tx group (bad-txns-non-v7-format from
MiniWallet).

Tier: V2 (fixup to v2/034)
